{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver never came within the pickup geofence. His own trace carries 64 fixes across the whole attempt and the CLOSEST of them is 517.41 m from the Bedok Interchange pickup pin, against a TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius of 150 m set by POL-NS-02 and the fee schedule - more than three times the radius. That is a margin no 25 m accuracy filter can bridge, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails and the cancellation fee is not chargeable to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02710", "EV-TRIP-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-02 requires at least 3 consecutive position fixes within the arrival radius in the 15 minutes before the cancellation. The derived arrival block records 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes out of 64 driver fixes, so on the clause's own words the driver 'never arrived', POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails, and the rider is entitled to a full refund of the cancellation fee. I note that the 25 m accuracy filter cannot change this: the nearest fix is 517.41 m out, so the fixes are evidence of absence on distance alone, not merely excluded for accuracy.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02710", "EV-TRIP-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The wrong-entrance clause cannot rescue this fee. POL-NS-03 is confined to a driver stationary outside the arrival radius but not more than 400 m from the pin, and the driver's nearest fix is 517.41 m away - 117 m beyond that ceiling. POL-NS-01 itself directs that where the stationary fixes lie more than 400 m from the pin the driver never arrived and POL-NS-02 governs, so no part of the driver's compensation route is open on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02710", "EV-TRIP-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if arrival were somehow established, the waiting period was never served: the effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 seconds - 0 in-geofence runs, longest qualifying run 0.0 s - against the free waiting period of 180 seconds in force for this trip under trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, a shortfall of 180 seconds. POL-NS-06 refunds the cancellation fee in full on that arithmetic alone, whether or not the rider was present. I note the 300 s figure in fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec is not the operative number here: that table is retained only to read records authored before policy version 2, and this record carries its own platform_policy.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02710", "EV-TRIP-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 'arrived' event at 22:48:55 is a false arrival marker under POL-NS-05. Every one of the 64 driver fixes is at least 517.41 m from the pin, so at the arrival timestamp the driver was necessarily more than 300 m away; the trace also shows distinct speeds of 57 to 63 km/h, i.e. a vehicle in motion on an arterial or expressway road, not a car waiting at a bay. Recomputing the waiting clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix yields no such fix anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-05 limb (ii) refunds the fee in full, permits no driver compensation, and requires a false-arrival event to be recorded against the driver in the ruling's referrals.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02710", "EV-GPS-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this pickup road in this window. EV-ADVIS-02710-01 is MISSING, carries no payload, and its admissibility weight is 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - I disclose that impairment, and the absence is itself citable. Because the advisory limb requires a present and populated advisory, POL-NS-06 limb (i) is unavailable and the driver's 0 seconds of dwell cannot be topped up to the 180 second minimum by summing separate in-geofence intervals.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02710-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.unavailable",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider was at the pickup and her own track says so: 54 fixes, all 54 qualifying, the farthest only 8.59 m from the pin and well inside the 200 m rider presence radius for a TRANSPORT_HUB. In candour, POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider as a whole on this record - the driver did reply, 30 seconds after her message, within the 120 second window, so limb (b) is not met and I do not rest the refund on that clause - but limb (c)'s presence finding stands and it contradicts the driver's counter-statement that 'the rider did not come'.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02710", "EV-CHAT-02710", "EV-TRIP-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.max_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log sets out the exchange the driver's own trace falsifies. At 22:49:35 the rider wrote 'where are you? i dont see any car'; at 22:50:05 the driver answered 'im here already'; the driver then cancelled at 22:53:55 without ever entering the geofence, his closest approach being 517.41 m. An assertion of presence in a message is not presence, and the trace matches the rider's account - the car was on another road, not at the pickup.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02710", "EV-GPS-02710", "EV-TRIP-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No driver compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. POL-NS-01 fails at limb (b), and POL-NS-05 limb (ii) and POL-NS-06 each independently displace the charge, so the driver's payout route is closed and the 4.50 must not be retained to fund it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02710", "EV-GPS-02710", "EV-TRIP-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The amount to be returned is the whole of the contested sum, 4.50 SGD. The fare ledger carries exactly one charge line - cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0 - and it reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd 4.50, so the refund is the cancellation-fee line only, with no booking or platform fee on this record to net off. A rider-filed dispute in which the whole contested amount is returned is a FULL_REFUND.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02710", "EV-TRIP-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing here needs a human reviewer, so no escalation should be ordered. The deciding facts - the driver's position and his dwell - are carried by EV-GPS-02710 and EV-TRIP-02710, both COMPLETE at weight 1.0, 100 percent coverage, no gaps and no issue codes, so the confidence cap under POL-GEN-02(2) is 1.0 and the 0.70 floor in POL-NS-09(a) is comfortably clear; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival under POL-NS-09(b); and the same-parties dispute counters read 0 for both rider and driver under POL-NS-09(c), with rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d of 0 under POL-NS-09(d). The only zero-weight artifact, the missing advisory, carries no fact and is relied on only for its absence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02710", "EV-TRIP-02710", "EV-RPROF-02710", "EV-DPROF-02710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii) — false-arrival record: the trip_record 'arrived' marker at 2026-08-19T22:48:55+08:00 on trip TRP-02710 was false (the driver's closest fix in EV-GPS-02710 is 517.41 m from the Bedok Interchange pin and there is no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip). Record a false-arrival event against driver DRV-09710 alongside the full refund of the 4.50 SGD cancellation fee."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver. The 4.50 SGD no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-02710 is refunded in full to the rider. No compensation is payable to the driver. The refund is the cancellation-fee line only: EV-FARE-02710 shows cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50 and refund_issued_sgd 0.0, so the whole contested sum of 4.50 SGD is returned, and 4.50 is below the 8.00 automatic-execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it executes on issue. WHY THE FEE DOES NOT STAND. A no-show fee needs all four limbs of POL-NS-01. Limb (b) fails and limb (c) fails with it. EV-GPS-02710 is a complete trace (100.0 percent coverage, 64 driver fixes, no gaps, weight 1.0) whose closest driver fix is 517.41 m from the Bedok Interchange pin — more than three times the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius — and it records 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying in-geofence run of 0.0 s, against the 180 s free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec). POL-NS-02 therefore finds no arrival, and POL-NS-06 refunds the fee on the dwell arithmetic alone, whether or not the rider was present; the traffic-advisory route that might have permitted separate intervals to be summed is unavailable because EV-ADVIS-02710-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) and POL-NS-06 requires a present and populated advisory. THE 'ARRIVED' EVENT. EV-TRIP-02710 does carry a driver arrival marker at 22:48:55 and a 5.0-minute wait timer running to the driver's termination at 22:53:55 under RIDER_NO_SHOW. That marker is a BUTTON press, which is the driver's own status rather than a platform geofence measurement; under POL-NS-05 it is FALSE because the trace puts the driver more than 300 m from the pin at that timestamp (in fact at least 517.41 m), and a false marker does not start the waiting clock. Because no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip, POL-NS-05(ii) refunds the fee in full, bars compensation and requires the false-arrival record carried in the referrals above. On the driver's claim that limbs (a) and (d) are satisfied: (a) records a marker whose falsity POL-NS-05 establishes, and (d) requires the termination to fall at or after the required dwell elapsed — a dwell that never ran — so (d) is not met either. The rider's companion claim that the driver's fixes are 517.41 m out, 117 m beyond POL-NS-03's 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling, is accepted: POL-NS-03 cannot rescue the fee, and POL-NS-01 itself sends a driver more than 400 m from the pin to POL-NS-02. NO ESCALATION. The driver's POL-NS-09(b) argument — that the trip record's arrival-and-wait record contradicts the trace and needs a human reviewer — is rejected. The conflict exists on the face of the record, but POL-NS-05 is the clause that resolves it: a button press more than 300 m from the pin is a false marker, and the clock is recomputed from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, of which there are none. POL-NS-09(b) requires a conflict that no clause resolves, so it does not fire. The other triggers do not fire either: the deciding facts rest on artifacts at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 (not the bundle mean) and the 0.70 floor is clear; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 for both parties; rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 2 is below 4, and 2 divided by 93 completed trips is 0.0215, below 0.08); and the trace, the 2-message chat log (matching chat_message_count 2) and the fare ledger (4.50 reconciling with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd 4.50) are unimpaired under POL-NS-08(a)-(d). POINT BY POINT ON THE REST. POL-NS-04 is not needed to decide this case, and both sides are right about why: the driver replied 'im here already' 30 seconds after the rider's 'where are you? i dont see any car', inside the 120-second window, so limb (b) of that clause fails and it exonerates no one — but that does not matter, because the rider wins on the driver's own trace. The rider's presence is nonetheless corroborated: her 54 fixes are all within 8.59 m of the pin, inside the 200 m TRANSPORT_HUB presence radius, which contradicts the driver's counter-statement that the rider did not come. That counter-statement carries no weight_multiplier, enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the cap, and is an assertion of arrival rather than presence — an assertion the driver's own trace falsifies, matching the rider's account that the car was on another road. POL-NS-07 pays the driver nothing: its precondition (POL-NS-01 satisfied in full) is absent and POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 displace the charge. POL-GEN-01 was respected on both sides: the lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags was mentioned only to say it may not be substituted for the trailing-30-day figure, and no adverse finding rests on any context-only profile field. Confidence is 0.95, capped at 1.0 by the two deciding artifacts (EV-GPS-02710 and EV-TRIP-02710), both at weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
